#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:15
msgid "Library Dependency Finder (LDF)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:17
msgid ""
"Library Dependency Finder is a core part of PlatformIO Build System that "
"operates with the C/C++ source files and looks for ``#include ...`` "
"directives to know what header directories to include for the compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:21
msgid ""
"In spite of the fact that Library Dependency Finder is written in pure "
"Python, it evaluates :ref:`ldf_c_cond_syntax` (``#ifdef``, ``if``, "
"``defined``, ``else``, and ``elif``) without calling ``gcc -E``. This "
"approach allows to significantly reduce the total compilation time. See :ref:"
"`ldf_mode` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:27
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:30
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:32
msgid "Library Dependency Finder can be configured from :ref:`projectconf`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:42
msgid "Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:44
msgid ""
"There are different storages where Library Dependency Finder looks for "
"libraries. These storages (folders) have priority and LDF operates in the "
"next order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:48
msgid ""
":ref:`projectconf_pio_lib_dir` - own/private library storage per project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:49
msgid ""
":ref:`projectconf_pio_libdeps_dir` - project dependency storage used by :ref:"
"`librarymanager`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:51
msgid ""
"\":ref:`projectconf_pio_core_dir`/lib\" - global storage per all projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:52
msgid "Library storages built into frameworks, SDKs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:57
msgid "Dependency Finder Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:59
msgid ""
"Library Dependency Finder starts work from analyzing source files of the "
"project (:ref:`projectconf_pio_src_dir`) and can work in the next modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:0
msgid "``off``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:63
msgid ""
"\"Manual mode\", does not process source files of a project and "
"dependencies. Builds only the libraries that are specified in manifests (:"
"ref:`library_json`, ``module.json``) or using :ref:`projectconf_lib_deps` "
"option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:0
msgid "``chain``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:69
msgid ""
"[**DEFAULT**] Parses ALL C/C++ source files of the project and follows only "
"by nested includes (``#include ...``, chain...) from the libraries. It also "
"parses C, CC, CPP files from libraries which have the same name as included "
"header file. **Does not evaluate** :ref:`ldf_c_cond_syntax`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:0
msgid "``deep``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:75
msgid ""
"Parses ALL C/C++ source files of the project and parses ALL C/C++ source "
"files of the each found dependency (recursively). **Does not evaluate** :ref:"
"`ldf_c_cond_syntax`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:0
msgid "``chain+``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:80
msgid ""
"The same behavior as for the ``chain`` but **evaluates** :ref:"
"`ldf_c_cond_syntax`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:0
msgid "``deep+``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:83
msgid ""
"The same behavior as for the ``deep`` but **evaluates** :ref:"
"`ldf_c_cond_syntax`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:85
msgid ""
"The mode can be changed using :ref:`projectconf_lib_ldf_mode` option in :ref:"
"`projectconf`. Default value is set to ``chain``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:90
msgid ""
"Once a library is picked by the LDF for the build process, all source files "
"according to its manifest file will be built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:94
msgid ""
"Usually, when the LDF appears to fail to identify a dependency of a library, "
"it is because the dependency is only referenced from a library source file, "
"and not a library header file (see example below). In this case, it is "
"necessary to either explicitly reference the dependency from the project "
"source or :ref:`projectconf` (:ref:`projectconf_lib_deps` option), or change "
"the LDF mode to \"deep\" (not generally recommended)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:101
msgid ""
"A difference between ``chain/chain+`` and ``deep/deep+`` modes. For example, "
"there are 2 libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:104
msgid "Library ``Foo`` with files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:106
msgid "``Foo/foo.h``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:107
msgid "``Foo/foo.cpp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:108
msgid "``Foo/extra.cpp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:110
msgid "Library ``Bar`` with files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:112
msgid "``Bar/bar.h``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:113
msgid "``Bar/bar.cpp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:0
msgid "Case 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:117 ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:126
msgid "``lib_ldf_mode = chain``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:118
msgid ""
"``Foo/foo.h`` depends on the ``Bar`` library (contains ``#include <bar.h>``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:119 ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:128
#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:137
msgid "``#include <foo.h>`` is located in one of the project source files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:121
msgid ""
"Here the nested includes (``project file > foo.h > bar.h``) and LDF will "
"find both libraries ``Foo`` and ``Bar``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:0
msgid "Case 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:127
msgid ""
"``Foo/extra.cpp`` depends on the ``Bar`` library (contains ``#include <bar."
"h>``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:130
msgid ""
"In this case, LDF will not find the ``Bar`` library because it doesn't know "
"about the CPP file (``Foo/extra.cpp``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:0
msgid "Case 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:135
msgid "``lib_ldf_mode = deep``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:136
msgid ""
"``Foo/extra.cpp`` depends on ``Bar`` library (contains ``#include <bar.h>``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:139
msgid ""
"Firstly, LDF finds the ``Foo`` library, then it parses all sources from the "
"``Foo`` library and finds ``Foo/extra.cpp`` that depends on ``#include <bar."
"h>``.  Secondly, it will parse all sources from the ``Bar`` library. This "
"operation continues until all dependencies will not be parsed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:148
msgid "Compatibility Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:150
msgid ""
"Compatibility mode allows one to control strictness of Library Dependency "
"Finder. If library contains one of manifest file (:ref:`library_json`, "
"``library.properties``, ``module.json``), then LDF check compatibility of "
"this library with real build environment. Available compatibility modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:156
msgid "Does not check for compatibility (is not recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:0
msgid "``soft``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:159
msgid ""
"[**DEFAULT**] Checks for the compatibility with :ref:"
"`projectconf_env_framework` from build environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:0
msgid "``strict``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:163
msgid ""
"Checks for the compatibility with :ref:`projectconf_env_framework` and :ref:"
"`projectconf_env_platform` from build environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:166
msgid ""
"This mode can be changed using :ref:`projectconf_lib_compat_mode` option in :"
"ref:`projectconf`. Default value is set to ``soft``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../librarymanager/ldf.rst:172
msgid "C/C++ Preprocessor conditional syntax"
msgstr ""

